    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggers the heap-double-free. The crash matches exactly:\n- `hb_vector_t<CFF::OpStr, 8u>::fini()` at `hb-vector.hh:63`\n- Called from `hb_vector_t<CFF::CFF1FontDictValues, 8u>::~hb_vector_t()` at `hb-vector.hh:44`\n- In `accelerator_templ_t::~accelerator_templ_t()` at `hb-ot-cff1-table.hh:1010`\n\nThe double-free occurs because `fini_deep()` frees the inner `OpStr` vector's heap allocation, then the compiler-generated destructor of `static_array` elements tries to free the same memory again.\n\nPoC created and verified: `poc.otf` (588 bytes) — a CID-keyed CFF1 font with 10 font dicts, each containing 12+ parsed ops to force the inner `hb_vector_t<OpStr>` past its 8-element `static_array`, triggering the shallow-copy aliasing bug on vector growth.",
